Your `Category[]`/`Brand[]` schema is already an **implicit** many-to-many (no explicit join model needed) — per `many-to-many-relations.mdx` (Implicit many-to-many relations, orm/v7), Prisma manages the relation table automatically.

Your error comes from treating it like an explicit join table. For implicit m-n, `connect` goes directly under `categories`, no `create`/nested `category` wrapper:

```ts
prisma.brand.create({
  data: {
    name,
    slug,
    userId: user,
    image: uploadedImage.secure_url,
    categories: {
      connect: [{ id: "ckzpl0del0014vcv2ctift2f1" }],
    },
  },
  include: { categories: true },
});
```

Use `connect` for existing categories, or `create: [{ name: ... }]` if creating new ones inline (per "Querying implicit many-to-many" in that doc).

